// ModelWeave Inference Protocol (mwip), version 1: the Engine service.
//
// Inference engines implement Engine; the ModelWeave gateway is the client.
// An Engine server is one registered instance: one model in one role (see
// registry.proto). It is the only way engines integrate with ModelWeave.
//
// Execution modes of a Generate call (GenerateRequest.disagg):
//
//   normal  the instance runs the whole request (a unified instance, or a
//           decode instance registered with normal = true).
//   split   prefill and decode run on two instances that share the request
//           id and pair through one of three KV handshakes:
//
//     push       the gateway sends the decode leg first. The decode instance
//                answers Accepted with its KV receiver and how much of the
//                prompt it already caches. The gateway then sends the prefill
//                leg with that receiver; the prefill instance pushes the KV
//                the decode instance lacks and ends with PrefillDone.
//     bootstrap  both legs are sent at once. The decode instance fetches the
//                KV from disagg.prefill.bootstrap_addr for disagg.room.
//     pull       the prefill leg runs first and ends with PrefillDone carrying
//                a KV handle, which the gateway gives to the decode leg.
//
// The KV transfer itself (RDMA, NIXL, Mooncake, ...) is the engines' own:
// the addresses in KVReceiver, KVHandle and bootstrap_addr are engine-defined.
//
// Messages may be large (a 1M-token prompt is about 5 MiB): engines must
// accept messages of at least 64 MiB.

